This function checks if a given string containing only square brackets has nested brackets. It iterates through the string to find all opening and closing bracket indices, then counts how many opening brackets have corresponding closing brackets that appear later in the string. If there are at least two such pairs, it returns True, indicating the presence of nested brackets; otherwise, it returns False.

