This function takes a string as input and replaces sequences of spaces with underscores or hyphens based on their length. If the sequence is longer than two spaces, it replaces them with a hyphen; otherwise, it replaces them with underscores. The function iterates through each character in the input string, tracking the start and end indices of sequences of spaces. When a non-space character is encountered, it checks the length of the space sequence and appends the appropriate replacement to the output string. Finally, it handles any trailing spaces that were not processed during the iteration.

=== code written from the explanation ===

